   130	unqualified. A live native counterexample showed a failed
   131	multi-operation request retaining its first INSERT. The adapter uses one modify
   132	operation, but that alone does not repair failure atomicity. A globally fenced,
   133	fail-closed managed writer is a future candidate, not an implemented guarantee.
   134	Power-loss durability remains unqualified. Successful concurrent conditional
   135	updates, cancellation during WHERE evaluation, clean restart and recovery after
   136	a read-triggered OOM are narrower observations than crash-safe writes.
   137	
   138	The common acceptance ledger and evidence live in [qualification](../../qualification/).
   139	The competing implementations retain the same full ten-goal target and entity,
   140	fact, history, graph, presence and command scale dimensions. Passing the small
   141	storage fixtures does not pass upstream conformance, the workload packet, large
   142	scale, recovery or the complete ten-goal system.
   143	
   144	## Schema-aware native SPARQL
   145	
   146	`makeQleverNativeQueries(client, scope).select(contract, parameters, build, options)`
   147	is a separate application-facing query surface. The builder authors SPARQL;
   148	it does not produce or compile Datalog. Existing Triplex schema attribute
   149	handles select the typed assertion payload and its committed temporal guards:
   150	
   151	```ts
   152	const Balance = Attribute.int64(":account/balance");
   153	const Account = EntityType.make("Account", {
   154	  attributes: { balance: Attribute.use(Balance) },
   155	});

